35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The pattern is clear. Broad tools requiring daily entry from everyone were quietly dropped. Narrow tools for one trade still run. We must fund the narrow, not the broad.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital line is frozen, but the software allowance has room. However, per-head licences climb with every department added.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, narrow tools are great, but if half the sites have no signal, even a simple app fails! Plus, our devs are busy until Q3!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the data confirms your suspicion. Eleven misrouted deliveries stem from duplicate records, not inexperience. We lose an hour daily copying data. This is a maintenance failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the data confirms the strain. Two clerks handle all units, repeating the same certificate requests. The coordination group is unfilled, forcing manual logs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Sakura, you are right. A tool without a signal is a ghost. But remember, the narrow tools survived because they were simple. Complexity invites abandonment.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, that is worrying. If the signal fails, the tool is useless. I just need to ensure the recurring costs stay within the software allowance.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, that’s a huge waste! If we stop copying, maybe we can fix the misrouted deliveries? I’m glad we found the root cause!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, stopping the copying is the first step. The misrouted deliveries prove the data is fragmented. We need a single source of truth to stop the bleeding.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, a single source of truth is useless if no one maintains it. The unfilled coordination posts mean the burden falls on the same two people.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you identify the human cost. The past shows that without a clear owner, even good tools die. We must choose a project with a dedicated steward.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Asuka, that is a valid concern. But if the fixed-fee work is stable, we might avoid the rising licence costs. I just need to know if the budget covers the initial setup.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Asuka, that’s tough! If the devs are busy and the signal is bad, how do we even start? I’m worried we’ll just promise dates we can’t keep!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the unfilled posts are the bottleneck. Without a dedicated owner, the single source of truth will rot. We need a tool that survives neglect, not one that demands constant attention.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree. The current setup relies on two people doing the work of a team. We need a solution that doesn’t depend on them staying.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, precisely. The past proves that tools demanding constant attention fail. We must select a solution that endures without heroic effort.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I worry the initial setup might exceed the allowance. If we choose fixed-fee work, the recurring costs stay predictable. I hope we avoid hidden renewal bills.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, I agree! If the signal drops, the app is useless. I’m glad we found the root cause!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, I agree. The data shows fragmentation causes daily loss. We need a tool that consolidates records without demanding constant manual entry.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, I agree. The past shows tools die without owners. We need a solution that survives neglect, not one demanding heroic effort.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
