60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: The past favors narrow, durable tools. A central repository for supplier records addresses fragmentation without demanding daily entry from everyone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I worry about the costs. Per-head licences climb, but fixed-fee work is stable. I hope the initial setup fits within the software allowance.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, I love the idea! But wait, if our devs are busy until Q3, who builds it? I’m worried we’ll miss the deadline again!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, the data proves the fragmentation. A central repository stops the copying and misrouted deliveries. It is the logical fix for the daily losses I track.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, a repository is only as good as its maintenance. If the coordination group remains unfilled, who updates the records? I need a clear owner.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the past shows narrow tools survive. A shared catalog with clear procedures is simpler than a complex app. It endures without heroic effort.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Asuka, I understand the risk. But if we use fixed-fee work, the recurring costs stay predictable. I just need to ensure the initial setup fits the allowance.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Asuka, that’s a fair point! But if we don’t fix the data mess, the rotas will keep breaking. I think the Hub is the best bet!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the Hub’s shared procedures distribute the load. It stops the daily copying and misrouted deliveries. It is the only option addressing the root cause I identified.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, distributing the load doesn't eliminate the need for oversight. If the coordination group stays unfilled, the Hub becomes another abandoned project. I need a guaranteed owner.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
